{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-affine}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4cf9bd999d480fb9cc2277d186d84a5c8fc2f8c0d781ecf4bb75a162edce27c2", "source_text": "Affine morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:809120492248df9bf87621b6d9bcab193f43e60b2b6ca7a80998d7fddf84b7f6", "unit_id": "tag:01S5:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:475749066e435e8b31bcc5f9d7b40d151153b0c2e16dd266f530fc9ad90b663e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c61a73f8f935cca797a127d28af9122c9c1e5429c4cb576c12b52a17fca69deb", "source_text": "A morphism of schemes <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>affine<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nthe inverse image of every affine open of <MATH_0002> is an affine\nopen of <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a3ca03d2744f09e2c7227023aefc43db649d715fa307664fe9410ad2e68daa4", "unit_id": "tag:01S6:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b86aad1a35fe18f72d1857a53f5a05ef281afd83ca3029332eb282edba653953", "source_text": "An affine morphism is separated and quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53ad16f4abedcaf259310c235dc5731ab6d3eb05949a0e633b0c6ca59d331314", "unit_id": "tag:01S7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$x_1, x_2 \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0006": "$W \\subset S$", "MATH_0007": "$s$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}(W)$", "MATH_0009": "$U = V = f^{-1}(W)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:909a5ab4e001d9be4917ca45f93b49b012cd86fcfa5c72039a6f8a6298bf36b9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bbd5865d491d1cf7bb18f037e34b8e2dd05598f9f946c114c4e6023309ce07f6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be affine. Quasi-compactness is immediate from\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe will show <MATH_0002> is separated using\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>. Let\n<MATH_0003> be points of <MATH_0004> which map to the same point <MATH_0005>.\nChoose any affine open <MATH_0006> containing <MATH_0007>. By assumption\n<MATH_0008> is affine. Apply the lemma cited with <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03a316ace9c99b0b878d1ab6bbc46d79daa8cc3abc965a4ff32bd048e1770f90", "unit_id": "tag:01S7:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II, Corollary 1.3.2]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup W_j$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(W_j)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\cong \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$X = \\underline{\\Spec}_S(f_*\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{constructions-section-spec}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4f63eafde911104fa246740965e7241bf5957418a134ec91db33feb8e0f7c252", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e1a7b96e3a95b4ce3caeb603a4b0808d67fbf2a30cc673eecaa5a3df6ae7177d", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is affine.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0003>\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is affine.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists a quasi-coherent sheaf of <MATH_0005>-algebras\n<MATH_0006> and an isomorphism\n<MATH_0007>\nof schemes over <MATH_0008>. See\nConstructions, Section <REF_0001> for notation.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nMoreover, in this case <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:636c36e0011afb64bc0761d71a962a4ef0ae6a95962e224787b90b8eec2f42d9", "unit_id": "tag:01S8:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01S5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} W_j$", "MATH_0002": "$f^{-1}(W_j)$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A} = f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0007": "$g : Y = \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\text{id} : \\mathcal{A} = f_*\\mathcal{O}_X \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0010": "$can : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$can|_{f^{-1}(W_j)} : f^{-1}(W_j) \\to g^{-1}(W_j)$", "MATH_0013": "$can$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-quasi-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-push-forward-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-canonical-morphism}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-spec-properties}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72293b044803fdd7e4740d3757e79265fcf2a9c7beb068bad711eea840f9770c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:21fc38fe7e92b42db1786e6c4438bbf31779f37cf273968ba884c9ec95c12f32", "source_text": "It is obvious that (1) implies (2).\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0001> is an affine open covering such that\neach <MATH_0002> is affine. By\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001> we see\nthat <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact. By\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe see the morphism <MATH_0004> is quasi-separated. Hence by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0003> the\nsheaf <MATH_0005> is a quasi-coherent sheaf\nof <MATH_0006>-algebras. Thus we have the scheme\n<MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008>.\nThe identity map\n<MATH_0009>\nprovides, via the definition of the relative spectrum,\na morphism <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011>, see\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nBy assumption and the lemma just cited\nthe restriction <MATH_0012>\nis an isomorphism. Thus <MATH_0013> is an isomorphism.\nWe have shown that (2) implies (3).\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nAssume (3). By Constructions, Lemma <REF_0005>\nwe see that the inverse image of every affine open is affine, and hence\nthe morphism is affine by definition.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:328f49ede5bb8767dbb3903af75055bc5a0e5571adea54f509ef862089407503", "unit_id": "tag:01S8:proof"}
